Sure, here's an example of a simple portfolio website for a Frontend Software Engineer using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Allam's Portfolio</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
        }
        header {
            background-color: #333;
            color: white;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 1rem 0;
        }
        nav {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-around;
            background-color: #4CAF50;
            padding: 0.5rem 0;
        }
        nav a {
            color: white;
            text-decoration: none;
        }
        .container {
            max-width: 1200px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 2rem;
        }
        h1, h2, h3 {
            color: #545454;
        }
        section {
            margin-bottom: 3rem;
        }
        .project {
            border: 1px solid #ccc;
            padding: 1rem;
            margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
        }
        footer {
            background-color: #333;
            color: white;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 0.5rem 0;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<header>
    <h1>Welcome to Allam's Portfolio</h1>
</header>

<nav>
    <a href="#about">About Me</a>
    <a href="#projects">Projects</a>
    <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
</nav>

<div class="container">

    <section id="about">
        <h2>About Me</h2>
        <p>I am a passionate Frontend Software Engineer with experience in building responsive and user-friendly websites. I have a strong background in HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and other web technologies.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="projects">
        <h2>Projects</h2>
        <div class="project">
            <h3>Project 1: My Portfolio Website</h3>
            <p>This is a simple portfolio website that showcases my skills and experiences as a Frontend Software Engineer.</p>
            <a href="#">View Project</a>
        </div>
        <div class="project">
            <h3>Project 2: Social Media App</h3>
            <p>A social media app built using React.js and Firebase. Users can create accounts, post updates, like posts, comment on them, and follow other users.</p>
            <a href="#">View Project</a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section id="contact">
        <h2>Contact Me</h2>
        <form>
            <label for="name">Name:</label>
            <input type="text" id="name" name="name"><br><br>
            <label for="email">Email:</label>
            <input type="email" id="email" name="email"><br><br>
            <label for="message">Message:</label><br>
            <textarea id="message" name="message"></textarea><br><br>
            <button type="submit">Send</button>
        </form>
    </section>

</div>

<footer>
    <p>&copy; 2021 Allam's Portfolio</p>
</footer>

</body>
</html>
```

Save this code in a file named `index.html` and open it in your web browser to view the portfolio. You can customize it further by adding more projects, editing the styles, or modifying the content.
